## SEVERITY / VERDICT (the grading rule is decided HERE; apply it, do not re-argue it)
*Blocker:* a path beyond the one; a product byte; a removed line other than the moved lines (base 74-85 less the kept blank line), or an edited moved line other than the stated rename; the new row RED at the unmutated head, c1 or c2; the head moved (a verdict is valid only at the head it ran on); a reproduced timing red (3 of 3 alone at the head, not at main); a NEW CodeQL alert at or above the ruleset's thresholds on the changed lines; a secret in this diff; a person's name, decision-card id, ticket key or mutant id in an added line or the commit message; a build warning (warnings-as-errors); a failing test at the head after the file is re-run alone twice and the red not reproduced at main. *Major (class "a pinned row that does not turn red under the defect it names, or turns red for another reason, or can fail only by timing"; REPORTED for a product-owner card, not a build round):* the row GREEN under N1, N2, N4, N8 or N10; the message pin not load-bearing (N6/N7); the new row red 1 or more of 20 alone at load1 below 7; a row red for another reason than its prediction on more than one variant; the row leaving a temporary folder after a green run or a red run inside the `try` (cell H); a builder claim contradicted by measurement with a verdict consequence (names not equal, 3163 not reproducing, the moved block not byte-equal modulo the rename, the removed-line set not the 11); a path shared with a live lane or another open PR. *Minor/Note:* N3 green (the row pins the 0 case; Note if the ticket names only that shape); N5 green (the existence check pinned by no row: a Note on the file, outside the ticket); the leak under S1 not caught by any row; `Guid.NewGuid()` in the added lines; the `libraries` entry left in the copy's deps.json; the test name differing from the brief's suggestion; the PR body's "5 of 5 runs" miscount, the ticket key and the generated-with line in the body; a PR title that differs from the commit subject; unsigned commit; the Co-Authored-By trailer; the audit-guards-the-pin observation (PCb) as a statement about the repo, not a defect of the row; the SDK 10.0.401 versus 10.0.403 gap (state it, never grade it); the gitleaks false positive in the untouched file; CodeQL PENDING at the verdict; Linux differences you cannot run. Say which rule you applied for every finding. **Round 1 of 2: do not pad a Note into a NO GO and do not soften a Blocker: quote the variant, the row and the number.** **VERDICT RULES.** GO needs Checks 1-4, 6 and 8 measured with their controls, the row GREEN at c0/c1/c2 and RED for the predicted reason under N1, N2, N4, N7, N8, N9, N10 (3 of 3 each), the message pin shown load-bearing, cell Z, cell H and the PCb question answered, CI predicate read, and every `Analyze (<language>)` run COMPLETE with the PR's open alerts zero (the alert read has no positive control: say so); GO WITH FINDINGS = Minor/Note/Condition only (including an open item named on the line above the last line); NO GO on any Blocker or Major of this PR, with the class named, "round 1 of 2" and the fix-shape in prose. A security-shaped finding you cannot classify is a STOP (hand to G1).
